Implement user story SKY-004-impl: Implement Express REST API server with /health, /search, /cheapest, and static dashboard route

## Story Description
Create src/server.ts — an Express HTTP server that exposes: (1) GET /health → { status: 'ok', uptime: number }, (2) GET /search?from=LHR&to=JFK&date=2026-08-01&adults=1 → { flights: FlightResult[], count: number, searchedAt: string }, (3) GET /cheapest?from=LHR&to=JFK&date=2026-08-01 → the single cheapest FlightResult or 404 JSON { error: string } if none found, (4) GET / → serves src/public/index.html by reading the file at runtime (fs.readFileSync). Server reads PORT from env (default 3000); reads RAPIDAPI_KEY from env and passes to SkyscannerClient. If RAPIDAPI_KEY is absent at startup all API routes return 503 { error: 'RAPIDAPI_KEY not configured' }; /health and / are never gated. The listen() call must be guarded so importing `app` in tests does not bind a port. Add 'start' script in package.json pointing to 'node dist/server.js'. The build script must copy src/public/ into dist/public/ as part of `npm run build` so the / route handler resolves correctly under both `tsx src/server.ts` and `node dist/server.js`. Depends on SKY-002 (SkyscannerClient and FlightResult type must exist).

## Acceptance Criteria
- Express server exports named `app` separately from `listen()` with main-module guard so supertest imports without binding a port
- GET /health returns HTTP 200 JSON { status: 'ok', uptime: <positive number> } regardless of RAPIDAPI_KEY presence
- GET / returns HTTP 200 text/html with body read from src/public/index.html at runtime (fs.readFileSync), never gated by RAPIDAPI_KEY
- GET /search validates required params (from, to, date), defaults adults to 1, returns { flights, count, searchedAt } or 400/500/503 as appropriate
- GET /cheapest validates required params, returns single cheapest FlightResult or 404/400/500/503 as appropriate
- RAPIDAPI_KEY absence short-circuits /search and /cheapest with 503 { error: 'RAPIDAPI_KEY not configured' }; /health and / unaffected
- SkyscannerClient errors return 500 without crashing or unhandled rejection; FlightResult type imported from SKY-002, not redeclared
- Build script copies src/public/ into dist/public/ so the / route handler resolves correctly under both `tsx src/server.ts` and `node dist/server.js`; package.json includes 'start' script pointing to 'node dist/server.js'





